# Localization

- User-facing strings live in [`src/i18n/ru.json`](src/i18n/ru.json) and [`src/i18n/en.json`](src/i18n/en.json)
- When adding or changing any interface copy, update **both** files in the same change — never ship one locale only
- Read strings with `t('section.key')` from `useLocale()`; do not hardcode UI text in components
- Identifiers, file names, and code stay in English; only visible copy is localized
- Add a matching `MessageKey` in [`src/i18n/locales.ts`](src/i18n/locales.ts) when introducing a new key
- Locales are `ru` and `en`; the locale menu item shows the current language name (`ру` / `en`) and cycles them
